# Set 2 · Q. No. 2 · Historicizing Constructionism: Is the Sex/Gender Distinction Itself Constructed?
@py pr_question 2 Q2

## The answer map
::: fig mindmap | The answer map: every branch is one numbered heading of the model answer below.
@note Tell the history of the idea that gender is made — from roles to identities to bodies — then test whether the sex/gender distinction itself is a social construction, using Laqueur and intersex research, and reach a reasoned verdict.
@ask HISTORICIZE social CONSTRUCTIONISM (Wollstonecraft → Butler); in the light of LAQUEUR and INTERSEX
@ask research, is the SEX/GENDER DISTINCTION itself a SOCIAL CONSTRUCTION?
